        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-15T22:11:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The point of I2C_PORT_ACCEL is to prevent to insert this code, when we know the BMI160 is using a SPI bus.\nGuarding with CONFIG_I2C is not enough, because CONFIG_I2C is always included as there is a least one i2c device (battery, other sensors) connected to the EC.",
      "parentUuid": "61a736d2_9ff22ae5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 171,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "33fac333c6c541d7845cfa9ad3f2c7d344f7c0ab",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e9e06766_65b47c6c",
        "filename": "driver/accelgyro_bmi_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-15T22:56:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I2C_PORT_ACCEL doesn\u0027t follow the pattern of other CONFIG_* options and isn\u0027t currently documented in config.h. Current board.h files are setting this to a specific I2C bus instance, but this driver doesn\u0027t actually check the value assigned so it\u0027s an inconsistent design.\n\nThe SPI/I2C bus designation is already required be setup in the motion_sensors[].i2c_spi_addr_flags, so both I2C_PORT_ACCEL and CONFIG_SPI_ACCEL_PORT are redundant in my opinion.\n\nIf all boards have I2C, then the I2C_PORT_ACCEL check only provides a small code size saving.  So my suggestion is to just remove I2C_PORT_ACCEL instead of renaming and documenting the macro in config.h\n\nBecause only a subset of boards enable SPI, having a guard on the SPI driver calls makes sense, but could be done with just CONFIG_SPI.  Again the cost is a small amount of code, but we get to delete a redundant config option.",
      "parentUuid": "1c768e29_3c659590",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 171,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "33fac333c6c541d7845cfa9ad3f2c7d344f7c0ab",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70bab8b6_df52ac29",
        "filename": "driver/accelgyro_bmi_common.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1104704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-16T01:59:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given the RAM/ROM size of current EC we have lost the priority to optimize for size, but running out of space has been a recurrent issue (see https://crbug.com/1034518 for last occurence).\nAseda has suggested a different approach that uses CONFIG_ variables at https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/353813.\nThe proposed change would eliminate SLAVE_IS_SPI as well, leading a small improvement on the data path.",
      "parentUuid": "e9e06766_65b47c6c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 171,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "33fac333c6c541d7845cfa9ad3f2c7d344f7c0ab",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
